{"id": "b73aef65-4dd1-48d3-bfc9-6d8e60a9a1e5", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"text": "I'll check your ECR lifecycle policy for `checkout-service` and look at CloudTrail for what actually deleted the `v3.1.0` tag, plus scan for other tags at risk.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "tooluse_OIMRNzRUQijtQbNlAX2Xme", "tool_name": "gather_context", "input": {"prompt": "{
  "task": "Determine whether an ECR lifecycle policy caused image tag v3.1.0 to be removed from the 'checkout-service' ECR repository, and identify what other tags in that repo are at risk of similar removal.",
  "context": "Customer reports that image tag v3.1.0 disappeared from ECR repo 'checkout-service' yesterday (around 2026-11-04), and their ECS service failed to start as a result (likely ImagePullBackOff / manifest not found due to missing tag). They want to know: (1) was the ECR lifecycle policy responsible for expiring/removing this tag, and (2) what other tags/images in the same repo are currently at risk of expiration under the same policy.",
  "resources": ["ECR repository: checkout-service", "AWS account: 012345678901_1", "region: us-east-1"],
  "timeframe": "2026-11-04T00:00:00Z/2026-11-05T15:30:34Z",
  "criteria": [
    "Fetch the ECR lifecycle policy for checkout-service (get_lifecycle_policy / describe) and evaluate its rules (e.g. expire untagged after N days, keep only last N tagged images matching a prefix pattern, age-based expiration).",
    "Check whether v3.1.0 matched any expiration rule (e.g. was it untagged, did it exceed a countNumber limit such as 'keep last 10 images', or exceed a countdays age threshold).",
    "Search CloudTrail (us-east-1) for ECR events like BatchDeleteImage, PutImage, or lifecycle policy execution events (ecr.amazonaws.com) referencing the checkout-service repository and v3.1.0 tag/digest in the 2026-11-04 to 2026-11-05 window, to confirm whether the deletion was triggered by the lifecycle policy (automated, actor = ecr lifecycle service) vs a manual/user-initiated BatchDeleteImage call.",
    "List current images/tags in checkout-service repo with push dates and tag counts, and against the lifecycle policy rules identify which other tags are close to being expired next (e.g. next in line to be evicted by a 'keep last N' rule, or approaching an age-based expiration threshold).",
    "Report the exact lifecycle policy rule text/JSON if one exists, and whether the repo also has a repository policy (access) that's unrelated — don't confuse access policy with lifecycle policy."
  ]
}", "deep_research": false}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Check ECR lifecycle policy and CloudTrail for checkout-service image deletion."}], "created_at": null}
